From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oliver Sargison <sarol263@student.otago.ac.nz>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 20:36:04 +1300
Subject: [PATCH 14/19] Plutonium: a page's popup keeps its opener, so OAuth
 sign-in works

What a preview's page opened was closed and its URL opened again in a fresh
tab. That tab had no window.opener, so a sign-in popup couldn't post its
result back, and the flow never finished.

- The tab the page opened now backs the new preview tab itself: the thread's
  next new preview tab adopts it instead of opening a blank one and loading
  the URL again.
- When it closes itself (window.close(), as sign-in popups do once they have
  reported back), its preview tab closes too and the opener's comes back to
  the front, as the popup window does in the Electron build.
- With several shell pages, only one asks for the preview tab (and closes
  it), through a Web Lock; before, each page opened one.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
